00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:57.360
The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,183, down 0.3%, while the NASDAQ Composite finished at 23,586,

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:09.300
down 0.6%. That NASDAQ closes up 1.51% year-to-date and up 5.42% since the practice portfolio opened on March 16th, 2026.

00:01:10.429 --> 00:01:20.549
The TSX composite rose 0.7% to 34,427, with tech names leading the North American recovery after recent AI stock weakness.

00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:27.249
Yes, about 14 days ago we picked CRT.UN and it closed plus 0.49%.

00:01:27.589 --> 00:01:33.489
Urste group, investing.com notes, raised Spotify to buy on strong revenue growth, which

00:01:33.489 --> 00:01:36.449
is a prompt to open the filings rather than to buy the headline.

00:01:36.989 --> 00:01:41.829
Pull the latest earnings release in your brokerage, compare year-over-year revenue growth with

00:01:41.829 --> 00:01:46.849
the prior two quarters, and confirm the upgrade arrived after at least one positive revision.

00:01:46.849 --> 00:01:46.949
traction.

00:01:47.429 --> 00:01:52.869
Track the exact revenue figure in the most recent 10Q or 10K, and note whether it exceeds

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:56.689
the 2-quarter average by at least 5% before you act on the rating.

00:01:57.329 --> 00:02:01.909
The method works when revenue acceleration precedes the rating move, and it fails when

00:02:01.909 --> 00:02:04.449
the upgrade shows up after the stock has already run.

00:02:04.989 --> 00:02:10.109
In past cycles, upgrades without that revenue confirmation produced flat or negative three-month

00:02:10.109 --> 00:02:12.289
returns once sector rotation shifted.

00:02:12.289 --> 00:02:17.189
It is like a landlord who only reprints the lease rate after two months of actual higher

00:02:17.189 --> 00:02:21.229
occupancy, not after a broker's flyer about the neighborhood getting hot.

00:02:21.829 --> 00:02:24.929
The upgrade is the flyer, the revenue line is the occupancy.

00:02:25.469 --> 00:02:31.149
You see a buy hit the tape, you open the 10Q, and revenue is not 5% above that 2-quarter

00:02:31.149 --> 00:02:31.549
average.

00:02:32.149 --> 00:02:34.009
Do you still buy the rating, or do you wait?

00:02:34.429 --> 00:02:34.789
I'd wait.

00:02:35.269 --> 00:02:39.809
The filter exists to keep you off the late upgrade, not to decorate a thesis you already

00:02:39.809 --> 00:02:40.229
wanted.

00:02:40.229 --> 00:02:46.009
Earth Day Group also resumed coverage on Johnson &amp; Johnson with a buy tied to its growth outlook,

00:02:46.369 --> 00:02:51.229
so the same revenue first check applies across sectors, not only in media or tech.

00:02:51.749 --> 00:02:56.689
Investors who ran that filter on Spotify last quarter would have seen the revenue line accelerate

00:02:56.689 --> 00:03:00.889
before the rating change appeared, and rating moves that follow revenue beats

00:03:00.889 --> 00:03:05.249
tend to attract follow-on institutional flows rather than front-running noise.

00:03:05.249 --> 00:03:10.529
run the check inside a tax-free savings account or TFSA or a registered

00:03:10.529 --> 00:03:16.269
retirement savings plan or RRSP to avoid tax drag on any short-term position.

00:03:16.889 --> 00:03:22.318
Remember, the rating is the headline. The revenue line is the evidence. Advanced

