00:08:13.964 --> 00:08:19.961
name. Shares in a newly listed AI name sit quiet for two weeks after the debut, then

00:08:19.961 --> 00:08:25.041
start sliding with no earnings miss on the tape. Insider lock up agreements block sales

00:08:25.041 --> 00:08:30.481
for 180 days after an initial public offering, and the first wave of supply hits on the

00:08:30.481 --> 00:08:32.681
expiration date written in the prospectus.

00:08:33.301 --> 00:08:38.181
Andthropic's expiration start December 15th, which means that restricted supply stretch

00:08:38.181 --> 00:08:43.061
ends then and additional tranches follow over subsequent months, with a flood of selling

00:08:43.061 --> 00:08:45.361
possible as those windows open in sequence.

00:08:46.081 --> 00:08:50.961
Set a calendar alert 30 days before each scheduled release and cut position size in advance

00:08:50.961 --> 00:08:52.921
rather than waiting for volume to spike.

00:08:53.641 --> 00:08:58.561
The common misconception is that an IPO debut price already reflects all future selling.

00:08:59.161 --> 00:09:03.781
The lock-up schedule is a predictable supply overhang that only appears once the restriction

00:09:03.781 --> 00:09:04.101
lifts.

00:09:04.921 --> 00:09:08.941
Ignore the calendar and you are competing against large blocks that hit the tape on the

00:09:08.941 --> 00:09:10.421
exact date the lock-up lifts.

00:09:10.421 --> 00:09:16.561
The same pattern has repeated across prior high-profile AI and tech listings, where the first

00:09:16.561 --> 00:09:21.301
post-lock-up session produced above-average volume and below-average returns for holders

00:09:21.301 --> 00:09:22.601
who stayed fully sized.

00:09:23.161 --> 00:09:28.241
A position-size reduction rule 30 days ahead turns that known supply event into a planned

00:09:28.241 --> 00:09:30.341
exit rather than an unexpected drop.

00:09:30.921 --> 00:09:33.381
The debut print is not a finished sale schedule.

00:09:34.081 --> 00:09:36.541
Models and agents covers the AI side daily.

00:09:36.541 --> 00:09:41.893
Open your brokerage screener, set a filter for NASDAQ tech names with today's volume

00:09:41.893 --> 00:09:47.173
above the 20 session average, and flag any that also appear on an analyst upgrade list.

00:09:47.713 --> 00:09:52.173
Review the top three results for five minutes each, and run the revenue first check on

00:09:52.173 --> 00:09:55.193
any upgrade that shows up before you even think about size.

